# JSI Zero-Copy Lazy-JSON Integration Plan

This document provides the **complete, production-ready implementation** for cross-compiling the `html_2_json` Rust library and integrating it into React Native using the **Lazy-JSON JSI Bridge** architecture.

### Why this design?
1. **Zero-Copy List Evaluation**: JavaScript only requests block data as they enter the screen viewport (e.g. inside a `FlatList`).
2. **Zero Boilerplate**: Instead of writing hundreds of C++ JSI mapping functions for every nested inline formatting tag, we serialize *only the requested block* into a tiny JSON string and parse it instantly inside Hermes.
3. **No Garbage Collection Pressure**: The JS engine only parses small single-block JSON payloads on-demand, keeping memory allocations near zero.

---

## 🗺️ Logical Order of Operations

```mermaid
graph TD
  A[1. Configure Cargo.toml] --> B[2. Implement ffi.rs in Rust]
  B --> C[3. Compile Native Binaries]
  C --> D[4. Set up C++ JSI HostObjects]
  D --> E[5. Mount JSI in React Native]
```

---

## 🛠️ Step 1: Cargo Configuration (`Cargo.toml`)

Update the library's `html_2_json/Cargo.toml` to define compilation targets:

```toml
[lib]
name = "html_2_json"
path = "src/lib.rs"
crate-type = ["staticlib", "cdylib"]  # staticlib (iOS .a), cdylib (Android .so)
```

---

## 🔗 Step 2: Implement the C FFI Boundary in Rust (`ffi.rs`)

We expose a flat C FFI from Rust. We serialize individual blocks by index to JSON on demand.

Create `html_2_json/src/ffi.rs`:

```rust
use std::ffi::{CString, CStr};
use std::os::raw::c_char;
use crate::models::ContentBlock;
use crate::parse_html;

// Opaque container representing the parsed article
pub struct ParsedArticle {
    pub blocks: Vec<ContentBlock>,
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn parse_html_ffi(html_ptr: *const c_char) -> *mut ParsedArticle {
    if html_ptr.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let c_str = unsafe { CStr::from_ptr(html_ptr) };
    let html = c_str.to_string_lossy();

    let blocks = parse_html(&html);
    Box::into_raw(Box::new(ParsedArticle { blocks }))
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn free_article_ffi(article: *mut ParsedArticle) {
    if !article.is_null() {
        unsafe { let _ = Box::from_raw(article); }
    }
}

// Get the total block count (for lazy length checking)
#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_block_count(article: *const ParsedArticle) -> usize {
    if article.is_null() { return 0; }
    unsafe { (*article).blocks.len() }
}

// Serialize only a single block by index (Lazy Evaluation)
#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_block_json(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> *mut c_char {
    if article.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    // Serialize only this specific block to JSON
    let block_json = serde_json::to_string(&blocks[index]).unwrap_or_default();
    CString::new(block_json).unwrap().into_raw()
}

// Free C-strings returned to C++ to avoid memory leaks
#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn free_string_ffi(s: *mut c_char) {
    if !s.is_null() {
        unsafe { let _ = CString::from_raw(s); }
    }
}
```

Make sure to export this module in your `html_2_json/src/lib.rs`:
```rust
pub mod ffi;
```

---

## 🛠️ Step 3: Compile the Binaries

Build the native binaries for both mobile operating systems:

### 3.1 Install Cross-Compilers
```bash
rustup target add aarch64-apple-ios x86_64-apple-ios-sim aarch64-apple-ios-sim
rustup target add aarch64-linux-android armv7-linux-androideabi i686-linux-android x86_64-linux-android
```

### 3.2 Build Commands
* **iOS (Static Libraries)**:
  ```bash
  cargo build --target aarch64-apple-ios --release
  cargo build --target aarch64-apple-ios-sim --release
  ```
* **Android (Shared Libraries)**:
  ```bash
  cargo install cargo-ndk
  cargo ndk -t arm64-v8a -o ./jniLibs build --release
  ```

---

## ⚡ Step 4: Write the C++ JSI HostObjects

Inside `cpp/HTMLParserHostObjects.h`, we write the JSI class that lazily deserializes individual blocks into JavaScript objects on-demand:

```cpp
#pragma once
#include <jsi/jsi.h>

extern "C" {
    // Rust FFI bindings
    struct ParsedArticle;
    ParsedArticle* parse_html_ffi(const char* html);
    void free_article_ffi(ParsedArticle* article);
    size_t get_block_count(const ParsedArticle* article);
    char* get_block_json(const ParsedArticle* article, size_t index);
    void free_string_ffi(char* s);
}

using namespace facebook;

class ArticleHostObject : public jsi::HostObject {
private:
    ParsedArticle* m_article;

public:
    ArticleHostObject(const char* html) {
        m_article = parse_html_ffi(html);
    }

    ~ArticleHostObject() {
        free_article_ffi(m_article);
    }

    jsi::Value get(jsi::Runtime& rt, const jsi::PropNameID& name) override {
        auto propName = name.utf8(rt);

        // article.length
        if (propName == "length") {
            return jsi::Value((int)get_block_count(m_article));
        }

        // article.getBlock(index)
        if (propName == "getBlock") {
            return jsi::Function::createFromHostFunction(
                rt, name, 1,
                [this](jsi::Runtime& rt, const jsi::Value& thisVal, const jsi::Value* args, size_t count) -> jsi::Value {
                    if (count < 1 || !args[0].isNumber()) {
                        throw jsi::JSError(rt, "getBlock expects a numeric index argument");
                    }

                    int index = args[0].asNumber();
                    char* raw_json = get_block_json(m_article, index);

                    if (raw_json == nullptr) {
                        return jsi::Value::null();
                    }

                    // Parse the single block JSON into a JS object using the engine's native parser
                    jsi::Value parsedBlock = rt.global()
                        .getPropertyAsObject(rt, "JSON")
                        .getPropertyAsFunction(rt, "parse")
                        .call(rt, jsi::String::createFromUtf8(rt, raw_json));

                    free_string_ffi(raw_json);
                    return parsedBlock;
                }
            );
        }

        return jsi::Value::undefined();
    }
};
```

---

## 🚀 Step 5: Mount JSI in React Native (JS Entry Point)

Register the global JSI function inside `cpp/html-parser.cpp`:

```cpp
#include "HTMLParserHostObjects.h"

void installHTMLParser(jsi::Runtime& jsiRuntime) {
    auto parseHTML = jsi::Function::createFromHostFunction(
        jsiRuntime,
        jsi::PropNameID::forAscii(jsiRuntime, "parseHTML"),
        1,
        [](jsi::Runtime& rt, const jsi::Value& thisVal, const jsi::Value* args, size_t count) -> jsi::Value {
            std::string html = args[0].asString(rt).utf8(rt);

            // Returns the HostObject wrapper
            return jsi::Object::createFromHostObject(rt, std::make_shared<ArticleHostObject>(html.c_str()));
        }
    );

    jsiRuntime.global().setProperty(jsiRuntime, "parseHTML", std::move(parseHTML));
}
```

In your React Native React Component:
```typescript
import React, { useMemo } from 'react';
import { FlatList, Text, View } from 'react-native';

const MyArticleComponent = ({ rawHtml }) => {
  // 1. Parses HTML to Rust memory synchronously with ZERO copying
  const article = useMemo(() => global.parseHTML(rawHtml), [rawHtml]);

  // 2. Wrap the host object with a lazy array accessor
  const dataList = Array.from({ length: article.length }, (_, index) => index);

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={dataList}
      keyExtractor={(index) => index.toString()}
      renderItem={({ item: index }) => {
        // 3. ONLY the rendered item is converted to a JS object inside Hermes!
        const block = article.getBlock(index);

        switch (block.type) {
          case 'Paragraph':
            return <Text>{block.children.map(c => c.text).join('')}</Text>;
          case 'Heading':
            return <Text style={{ fontSize: 20 }}>{block.children[0].text}</Text>;
          case 'Separator':
            return <View style={{ height: 1, backgroundColor: '#ccc' }} />;
          default:
            return null;
        }
      }}
    />
  );
};
```

# JSI Pure HostObject Integration Plan

This document outlines the **complete, production-ready implementation** for integrating `html_2_json` into React Native using **Pure JSI HostObjects**. 

We do **not** use JSON serialization or string copying. JavaScript holds references to C++ HostObjects, which query the Rust memory address space directly using a C-compatible FFI interface.

---

## 🛠️ Step 1: Cargo Configuration (`Cargo.toml`)

Update the library's `html_2_json/Cargo.toml` to specify static and dynamic compilation:

```toml
[lib]
name = "html_2_json"
path = "src/lib.rs"
crate-type = ["staticlib", "cdylib"]
```

---

## 🔗 Step 2: Implement the C FFI Boundary in Rust (`ffi.rs`)

Expose the `ParsedArticle` opaque struct and the exhaustive getters required for JSI to walk the entire AST tree on demand.

Create `html_2_json/src/ffi.rs`:

```rust
use std::ffi::{CString, CStr};
use std::os::raw::c_char;
use crate::models::{ContentBlock, InlineNode, TableCell, TableRow};
use crate::parse_html;

// Opaque container to pass across the FFI boundary
pub struct ParsedArticle {
    pub blocks: Vec<ContentBlock>,
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn parse_html_ffi(html_ptr: *const c_char) -> *mut ParsedArticle {
    if html_ptr.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let c_str = unsafe { CStr::from_ptr(html_ptr) };
    let html = c_str.to_string_lossy();

    let blocks = parse_html(&html);
    Box::into_raw(Box::new(ParsedArticle { blocks }))
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn free_article_ffi(article: *mut ParsedArticle) {
    if !article.is_null() {
        unsafe { let _ = Box::from_raw(article); }
    }
}

// ── Article Getters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_block_count(article: *const ParsedArticle) -> usize {
    if article.is_null() { return 0; }
    unsafe { (*article).blocks.len() }
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_block_type(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> *mut c_char {
    if article.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let type_str = match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::Paragraph { .. } => "Paragraph",
        ContentBlock::Heading { .. } => "Heading",
        ContentBlock::Image { .. } => "Image",
        ContentBlock::Figure { .. } => "Figure",
        ContentBlock::CodeBlock { .. } => "CodeBlock",
        ContentBlock::List { .. } => "List",
        ContentBlock::Table { .. } => "Table",
        ContentBlock::Quote { .. } => "Quote",
        ContentBlock::DefinitionList { .. } => "DefinitionList",
        ContentBlock::Video { .. } => "Video",
        ContentBlock::Audio { .. } => "Audio",
        ContentBlock::Embed { .. } => "Embed",
        ContentBlock::Separator { .. } => "Separator",
    };

    CString::new(type_str).unwrap().into_raw()
}

// ── Heading & Block Field Getters ───────────────────────────────────────────

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_heading_level(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> u8 {
    if article.is_null() { return 0; }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return 0; }

    match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::Heading { level, .. } => *level,
        _ => 0,
    }
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_image_url(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> *mut c_char {
    if article.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let url = match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::Image { url, .. } => url.clone(),
        ContentBlock::Figure { url, .. } => url.clone(),
        _ => "".to_string(),
    };

    CString::new(url).unwrap().into_raw()
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_image_alt(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> *mut c_char {
    if article.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let alt = match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::Image { alt, .. } => alt.clone().unwrap_or_default(),
        ContentBlock::Figure { alt, .. } => alt.clone().unwrap_or_default(),
        _ => "".to_string(),
    };

    CString::new(alt).unwrap().into_raw()
}

// ── CodeBlock Getters ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_codeblock_code(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> *mut c_char {
    if article.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let code = match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::CodeBlock { code, .. } => code.clone(),
        _ => "".to_string(),
    };

    CString::new(code).unwrap().into_raw()
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_codeblock_lang(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> *mut c_char {
    if article.is_null() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return std::ptr::null_mut(); }

    let lang = match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::CodeBlock { language, .. } => language.clone().unwrap_or_default(),
        _ => "".to_string(),
    };

    CString::new(lang).unwrap().into_raw()
}

// ── Inline Node Getters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn get_block_child_count(article: *const ParsedArticle, index: usize) -> usize {
    if article.is_null() { return 0; }
    let blocks = unsafe { &(*article).blocks };
    if index >= blocks.len() { return 0; }

    match &blocks[index] {
        ContentBlock::Paragraph { children } => children.len(),
        ContentBlock::Heading { children, .. } => children.len(),
        _ => 0,
    }
}

// ── Memory Cleanup ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn free_string_ffi(s: *mut c_char) {
    if !s.is_null() {
        unsafe { let _ = CString::from_raw(s); }
    }
}
```

